<h2>Why FluxEncoder Exists</h2>
<p>
  <a href="https://ffmpeg.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FFmpeg</a> is one of the most foundational software tools in media engineering. Its command-line surface exposes hundreds of muxers, codecs, pixel formats, and filter graphs, while its raw standard error stream mixes banner diagnostics, stream mappings, and high-frequency progress counters.
</p>
<p>
  FluxEncoder does not replace or obscure FFmpeg. Instead, it acts as a deterministic control and telemetry layer around FFmpeg and FFprobe:
</p>

